              "text": "えきべん (ekiben) is Sino-Japanese (kango): two Chinese characters read with their on'yomi, readings borrowed from Chinese. They are eki, \"station\" (Middle Chinese yek), and ben, the first sign of bentō, \"a boxed lunch\", a word whose older history is not settled (JMdict, KANJIDIC2; Middle Chinese in Baxter's transcription)."
            }
